virglrenderer: report the host's sampler limit

What: caps.v2.max_texture_samplers was always PIPE_MAX_SAMPLERS (32). It is now
the smallest texture unit limit of the shader stages the host has (fragment,
vertex, geometry, tessellation, compute), at most 32; a failed query is skipped.
Why: current guest Mesa takes this cap as every stage's sampler limit
(GL_MAX_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS). The Mac has 16 per stage, so a guest program
that used the reported 32 (dEQP-GLES3 sampler tests do) failed to link on the
Mac ("Implementation limit of 16 active fragment shader samplers exceeded") and
stopped the guest context. GLES 3.0 needs 16, so the guest loses nothing it
could use. One number for all stages: a host with more units in one stage than
another gives the guest the smaller number everywhere.
Upstreamable; not sent (upstream's comment says the value is no longer used,
but Mesa 26's virgl driver does use it).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-sampler-limit.c (fills the caps on the Mac's OpenGL and
compares with every stage's limit; fails without this patch).
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -13550,8 +13550,30 @@
     *
     * Now we send the "correct" value, to ensure good behavior from old guest
     * drivers, but it is not "useful" for any other purpose.
+    *
+    * Current guest Mesa takes it as every stage's sampler limit, so it must
+    * not exceed the host's for any stage the host has: macOS has 16, and a
+    * program with more samplers fails to link on the host. A query that
+    * fails (0) leaves the limit as it is.
     */
    caps->v2.max_texture_samplers = PIPE_MAX_SAMPLERS;
+   {
+      GLenum stage_limits[] = {
+         GL_MAX_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS, GL_MAX_VERTEX_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS,
+         has_feature(feat_geometry_shader) ? GL_MAX_GEOMETRY_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS : GL_NONE,
+         has_feature(feat_tessellation) ? GL_MAX_TESS_CONTROL_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS : GL_NONE,
+         has_feature(feat_tessellation) ? GL_MAX_TESS_EVALUATION_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS : GL_NONE,
+         has_feature(feat_compute_shader) ? GL_MAX_COMPUTE_TEXTURE_IMAGE_UNITS : GL_NONE,
+      };
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(stage_limits); i++) {
+         GLint units = 0;
+         if (stage_limits[i] == GL_NONE)
+            continue;
+         glGetIntegerv(stage_limits[i], &units);
+         if (units > 0 && (uint32_t)units < caps->v2.max_texture_samplers)
+            caps->v2.max_texture_samplers = units;
+      }
+   }
 
    if (has_feature(feat_ubo)) {
       glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_UNIFORM_BLOCK_SIZE, &max);
